===== sruman --help
Steam Linux Runtime manager: install and update runtimes, run native games in them through profiles and prefixes

Usage: sruman [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  sync         Refresh the sync index
  install      Install runtimes, with their dependencies
  upgrade      Upgrade installed runtimes (all, or the named ones)
  outdated     Installed runtimes with a newer build in the sync index
  remove       Remove runtimes
  search       Search runtimes, or their packages
  info         Show a runtime: build, channel, sizes, dependencies, users
  runtimes     List installed runtimes
  builds       List a runtime's builds on the server
  files        List an installed build's files
  verify       Check installed builds against their file lists (all without arguments)
  clean        Clean the download cache and old builds
  import       Install from local archives or directories
  run          Run a game from games.toml
  execute      Run an executable once with a profile
  shell        Open a shell in a profile's runtime and prefix
  status       Show running games and sessions
  stop         Stop games, profiles' sessions or processes
  killall      Stop everything sruman started
  list         List games
  show         Show a game: executable, profile, runtime, prefix, environment
  check        Check games and profiles without launching (all without arguments)
  logs         Print a game's latest run log
  init         Create or update a profile's prefix
  profiles     Manage profiles
  steam        Run Steam on sruman's runtimes: replace Steam's own copies with links to the same builds
  provide-umu  Make a runtime umu's folder under `$XDG_DATA_HOME/sruman/umu/`, so umu runs it instead of downloading its own
  doctor       Check user namespaces, bubblewrap and the runtimes
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -y, --yes
          Answer every prompt with its default

      --color <WHEN>
          Colorize the output
          
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

  -q, --quiet
          Less output (`runtimes`: names only)

  -v, --verbose...
          Log to stderr (-vv: more)

      --config <FILE>
          Use this config.toml

  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version

===== sruman sync --help
Refresh the sync index

Usage: sruman sync [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --force
          Refetch even if nothing changed on the server

  -y, --yes
          Answer every prompt with its default

      --color <WHEN>
          Colorize the output
          
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

  -q, --quiet
          Less output (`runtimes`: names only)

  -v, --verbose...
          Log to stderr (-vv: more)

      --config <FILE>
          Use this config.toml

  -h, --help
          Print help

===== sruman install --help
Install runtimes, with their dependencies

Usage: sruman install [OPTIONS] <RUNTIMES>...

Arguments:
  <RUNTIMES>...
          Runtimes, optionally pinned: `sniper` or `sniper=<build>`

Options:
      --needed
          Skip runtimes that are installed already

  -y, --yes
          Answer every prompt with its default

      --color <WHEN>
          Colorize the output
          
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      --download-only
          Download without installing

  -q, --quiet
          Less output (`runtimes`: names only)

  -v, --verbose...
          Log to stderr (-vv: more)

      --config <FILE>
          Use this config.toml

  -h, --help
          Print help

===== sruman upgrade --help
Upgrade installed runtimes (all, or the named ones)

Usage: sruman upgrade [OPTIONS] [RUNTIMES]...

Arguments:
  [RUNTIMES]...
          

Options:
      --sync
          Refresh the sync index first

  -y, --yes
          Answer every prompt with its default

      --allow-downgrade
          Go back to the channel's build when an installed one is newer

      --color <WHEN>
          Colorize the output
          
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      --download-only
          Download without installing

  -q, --quiet
          Less output (`runtimes`: names only)

  -v, --verbose...
          Log to stderr (-vv: more)

      --config <FILE>
          Use this config.toml

  -h, --help
          Print help

