===== sruman steam --help
Run Steam on sruman's runtimes: replace Steam's own copies with links to the same builds

Usage: sruman steam [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  status  Steam's runtimes: linked to which build, or Steam's own copy
  link    Replace Steam's runtimes with links to the same builds, importing Steam's copy of a build sruman doesn't have. Steam must not run
  unlink  Put copies of the builds back in place of the links. Steam must not run
  verify  Check the builds Steam links to against their file lists
  clean   Remove builds Steam updated in place and no longer links to
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -y, --yes
          Answer every prompt with its default

      --color <WHEN>
          Colorize the output
          
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

  -q, --quiet
          Less output (`runtimes`: names only)

  -v, --verbose...
          Log to stderr (-vv: more)

      --config <FILE>
          Use this config.toml

  -h, --help
          Print help

